@startuml
' The one value object the whole package agrees on.
'
' Everything else is a way of producing a SeoData, or a way of turning one into
' markup. It is readonly and normalises on construction, so a consumer can trust
' every property it reads.

title SeoData — the value object

skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #ffffff
  BorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #475569
}
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class "SeoData" <<final readonly>> {
  --
  + ?string $title
  + ?string $description
  + ?string $imageUrl
  + ?string $imageAlt
  + ?string $canonicalUrl
  + string $robots
  + string $type
  + ?string $siteName
  --
  + make(array $overrides) : SeoData
  + merge(array $overrides) : SeoData
  + isIndexable() : bool
  + toArray() : array
  --
  {static} ROBOTS_INDEX_FOLLOW
  {static} ROBOTS_NOINDEX_FOLLOW
  {static} ROBOTS_NOINDEX_NOFOLLOW
  {static} TYPE_WEBSITE
  {static} TYPE_ARTICLE
  {static} TYPE_PROFILE
}

class "Text" <<helpers>> {
  --
  {static} DESCRIPTION_LENGTH
  --
  + plain(?string) : string
  + truncate(?string, int) : ?string
  + excerpt(?string, int) : ?string
  + fromMarkdown(?string, int) : ?string
}

note bottom of SeoData
  __Normalised on construction__
  * blank strings become null
  * everything is trimmed
  * the description is held to
    Text::DESCRIPTION_LENGTH

  __merge()__ applies only the
  non-null entries of its
  argument, which is what makes
  layering fallbacks safe.
end note

SeoData ..> Text : truncates the description with

@enduml
